WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:06.310
In 1730, members of the Bishnoi community
gave their lives to protect trees.

2
00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:11.840
In 1973, villagers in the Himalayan
foothills hugged trees to stop them being

3
00:00:11.890 --> 00:00:13.000
felled.

4
00:00:13.050 --> 00:00:15.830
Today, at a temple farm in Hertfordshire,

5
00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:19.940
cows are never slaughtered
and oxen plough the land.

6
00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:24.040
Meanwhile, many sacred rivers
are badly polluted by sewage,

7
00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:26.610
factory waste and plastic.

8
00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:31.840
Why would anyone care for old cows,
and for rivers they call mothers?

9
00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:36.210
In this mission, you'll find out
why many Hindus call the cow mother,

10
00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:38.630
and what happens in a cow shelter.

11
00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:42.980
Then you'll weigh up different Hindu
views on protecting the environment.

12
00:00:43.030 --> 00:00:48.270
Your mission: find out what moves many
Hindus to care for cows and rivers.
